                <description><![CDATA[<p>A week or so ago I had the opportunity to speak to some high school kids as part of my friend Makiko’s <a href="https://spice.fsi.stanford.edu/fellowship/stanford-e-entrepreneurship-us">program</a>. I always love talking with them. They are super smart, don’t let things slide, and always push me.</p>
<p>Often when I am in these situations I go into a fugue state and whatever I have been thinking about for the last couple weeks surfaces. A severe case of recency bias.</p>
